       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. I know of no indication that supports it, and you haven't given a rationale. In a 70 kg patient with normal organ function, a sustained dose that high carries a real risk of serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and arrhythmia. I'm not comfortable being the one to place it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** Examples are 100 mg or 200 mg once daily, or a titration schedule. Tell me the dose you want.\n- **Enter the order with a flag for pharmacy review.** This applies if you want something above 200 mg/day for a specific reason. Give me the dose and rationale, and I'll put them in the note.\n- **Place the order directly yourself.** If you decide 1000 mg is warranted, you can do that through the standard system, where pharmacy and nursing safety checks will apply.\n\nIf this was meant to be a different dose, tell me and I'll enter it now."
